{"id":19,"date":"2023-02-14T23:48:16","date_gmt":"2023-02-15T04:48:16","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/sites.mit.edu\/grad-union\/home\/"},"modified":"2026-11-05T17:18:00","modified_gmt":"2026-11-05T22:18:00","slug":"home","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/grad-union.mit.edu\/","title":{"rendered":"Home"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cp-content-containers has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-4c607ce1 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"background-color:#f2f2f2;padding-right:75px;padding-left:150px\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignwide is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-794e3cfa wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\" style=\"padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Representatives of MIT and the MIT Graduate Student Union (GSU) have met 17 times since April 2026 to work together toward a new contract. This website provides a series of resources related to MIT\u2019s ongoing negotiations with the GSU:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cp-red-link is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\" style=\"border-bottom-color:#d8d8d8;border-bottom-width:1px\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/grad-union.mit.edu\/overview\/\" data-type=\"page\" data-id=\"30\"><strong>A statement of our principles<\/strong><\/a><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/grad-union.mit.edu\/key-issues\/\" data-type=\"page\" data-id=\"29\"><strong>A summary of key issues<\/strong><\/a><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/grad-union.mit.edu\/background-faq\/\" data-type=\"page\" data-id=\"28\"><strong>Answers to common questions<\/strong><\/a><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/grad-union.mit.edu\/negotiation-updates\/\" data-type=\"page\" data-id=\"24\"><strong>Updates on the negotiations to date<\/strong><\/a><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/grad-union.mit.edu\/community-updates\/\" data-type=\"page\" data-id=\"824\"><strong>Community updates<\/strong><\/a><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Throughout this process, MIT has been guided by its responsibility to provide the best possible educational and research experiences for all of its students, an obligation that is at the heart of our mission as an academic institution.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We will work to serve the collective best interests of every MIT student \u2014 the 3,300 students who are represented by the GSU, as well as the 8,700 students who are not \u2014 and will strive to reach an agreement that supports our students while advancing MIT\u2019s academic and research missions.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large cp-home-img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"722\" src=\"https:\/\/grad-union.mit.edu\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/home-hero-1024x722.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"wp-image-21\" srcset=\"https:\/\/grad-union.mit.edu\/files\/2025\/12\/home-hero-1024x722.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/grad-union.mit.edu\/files\/2025\/12\/home-hero-300x212.jpg 300w, https:\/\/grad-union.mit.edu\/files\/2025\/12\/home-hero-768x542.jpg 768w, https:\/\/grad-union.mit.edu\/files\/2025\/12\/home-hero.jpg 1242w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<!--